I wouldn't want a boy to carry a thing like this.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.510
on his conscience. Neither would I, Mr. Cleaver.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:10.780
Come along, Beaver. June, we're home.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.960
Son, I think you'd better go on upstairs and get at your homework.

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:20.850
You do believe me, don't you, Dad? Yes, Beaver, I do.

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.600
Do you believe me because I'm telling the truth

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:28.740
or just because I'm your kid? I expect us a little bit of both.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:31.020
Thanks, Dad.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:34.960
Well, did you get everything straightened out?

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:37.650
No, we just got everything a little more complicated.

00:17:39.270 --> 00:17:41.610
Kenneth made a very convincing little speech

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:44.370
about how he'd never even seen these things before,

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:46.020
and his father backed him up.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:49.890
Well, Ward, I'm not gonna let anything like this happen.

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:51.350
I'm gonna go down to that school tomorrow,

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:54.910
and I'm gonna tell Miss Landers what a liar and a thief this Kenneth is.

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:56.610
June, you can't do that.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.800
It's Beaver's word against his.

00:17:59.040 --> 00:17:59.980
Well, Ward, do you want...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.340
Do you want Kenneth to get away with this?

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:04.160
No, but why don't we wait a couple of days

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:06.580
and see if maybe Kenneth doesn't come around by himself.

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:09.920
Oh, Ward, I just think this is terrible.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:12.320
Why do we have to have a problem like this?

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:16.300
Well, it could be worse. We could have Kenneth.

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:23.560
Hey, Beaver, I'm waiting for you.

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:26.580
Be it, Kenneth, but I want to talk to you.

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:29.180
I don't want to talk to you, you rat.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:33.290
Why didn't you tell your father the truth?

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.760
Gee, I couldn't.

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:36.670
Why not?

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.120
But you don't know what it's like around my house.

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:43.560
Every time I do something bad, my father starts hollering and yelling at me.

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:47.740
And then he calls my mother down, and she starts hollering and yelling at me.

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:49.640
And I got a big sister.

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:53.120
Then when they stop, she starts hollering and yelling at me.

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:58.460
But you're a real rat, swiping stuff and then give it to me so I get in trouble.

00:18:58.640 --> 00:18:59.420
I'm sorry.

00:18:59.640 --> 00:18:59.960
I didn't...

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.300
was gonna come out that way.

00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:02.900
I'm just gonna go to Miss Landers

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:03.960
and tell her who's really been

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:05.000
swamming all that stuff.

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:07.480
Boy, Beaver, that'll be squealing.

00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:09.460
Well, it is not squealing

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.360
when you're squealing on a rat like you.

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:14.550
All right, Beaver, I'll do it.

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:15.690
Do what?

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:17.460
I'll go to Miss Landers

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:18.560
and squeal on myself.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:21.840
Well, okay.

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:23.610
But I'm gonna be there

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:24.630
so you don't do any squealing

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:25.530
in your own favor.

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:49.370
Yeah, they called off basketball practice.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.490
The coach said we were getting stale.

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:53.330
I think he had a date or something.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:55.720
Wally, don't you want something to eat?

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:59.200
No, uh, Eddie Haskell and I stopped by the bakery

00:19:59.200 --> 00:19:59.960
and got some day-old...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:06.710
eclairs to eat on the way home day-old eclairs were they all right well the whipped cream was a

00:20:06.710 --> 00:20:14.590
little sour but after three or four you don't notice it hey mom how's the beaver doing with

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:19.360
that new friend of his did he come home with any more loot today wally i wish you wouldn't joke

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:25.460
about that you know this is a very serious matter yeah i know mom but it's kind of funny the way

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:27.360
Beaver always believes crazy stuff.

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:35.410
I told my father I didn't steal the stuff.

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:37.420
And I told Beaver's father, too.

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:40.550
But I really did steal the stuff and give it to Beaver.

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:42.590
Did I leave anything out, Beaver?

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:45.170
Yeah, you left out about the fountain pen.

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:47.900
Oh, yeah. I also took a fountain pen

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:49.620
from one of the sixth-grade lockers.

00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:54.200
Well, I think the first thing, Beaver,

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:56.160
is for you to bring the things in

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:57.980
so that we can return them to the owners.

00:20:58.350 --> 00:20:59.410
Yes, Miss Landers.

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:04.100
And, Kenneth, I'm glad you finally told the truth.

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:07.820
Do you realize how serious this is?

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:12.100
Stealing from your classmates and then trying to put the blame on Beaver?

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:15.040
Yes, ma'am. I'm awful sorry.

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:18.240
But I didn't give the stuff to Beaver to get him blamed.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:20.920
What other reason could it be?

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:25.260
Well, I stole the stuff and gave it to Beaver

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:27.170
because I wanted him to like me.

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:29.960
You wanted a friend so bad...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:30.920
that you'd steal?

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:34.670
You don't know how it is, Miss Landers.

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:37.370
Beaver's the kind of guy that everybody likes him

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:38.390
just for doing nothing.

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:41.830
I say hello, and the guys tell me to get lost.

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:45.330
You can't make friends by stealing, Kenneth.

00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:53.240
Miss Landers, are you gonna tell the kids I'm a crook?

00:21:53.380 --> 00:21:57.360
I don't think that's necessary, Kenneth,

00:21:57.480 --> 00:21:59.620
but I will have to turn this matter over to the principal.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:05.230
And the very first thing I want you to do is to tell your father the truth.

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:09.410
Gee, I can't do that, Miss Landers.

00:22:09.780 --> 00:22:11.800
If I did, he'd hate me.

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:15.620
And the worst person in the whole world to have hate you is your father.

00:22:16.860 --> 00:22:19.460
Yeah, I guess that's because you have to be around him so much.

00:22:20.340 --> 00:22:26.350
Well, Kenneth, maybe I could ask your father to come in.

00:22:26.720 --> 00:22:29.960
And maybe I could explain it to him in a way that wouldn't upset him quite so.

00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:32.280
Gee, would you, Miss Landers?

00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:36.640
Well, I'll certainly try. After all, that's what friends are for.

00:22:37.300 --> 00:22:40.210
You mean you're my friend? I'd like to be.

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:45.270
How could you be my friend after I stole stuff and made all this trouble?

00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:47.920
I thought teachers only liked the good kids.

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:50.720
Oh, Kenneth, teachers like all of their students,

00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:54.780
but they feel a certain obligation to the ones who get into trouble

00:22:54.780 --> 00:22:56.960
because they're the ones that need our help.

00:22:57.930 --> 00:22:59.970
I never thought my first friend in school would be...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:08.090
be a teacher oh I think beaver's your friend too aren't you beaver yeah well I guess so but he

00:23:08.090 --> 00:23:13.780
better not start messing around with any lockers again oh I won't do that again in a hundred million

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.590
years well you better behave yourself Kenneth and I think you'll find that the way to make friends

00:23:20.590 --> 00:23:26.810
is not by giving them things but by giving them a little of yourself yes miss Lenders

00:23:41.840 --> 00:23:46.200
Isn't it amazing the lengths that Kenneth went to to have people like him?

00:23:46.890 --> 00:23:47.870
Yeah, I suppose so.

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:52.940
But then again, it's the great American dream today to be popular.

00:23:53.770 --> 00:23:55.760
Look at Fred Rutherford down at the office.

00:23:55.880 --> 00:23:59.280
He spends half his time worrying what the girls around the water cooler are saying about him.

00:24:00.092 --> 00:24:01.312
What do they say about him?

00:24:02.652 --> 00:24:04.992
Well, you know, I think if he knew what they really say, he'd kill himself.

00:24:07.580 --> 00:24:09.280
You know, when I was at boarding school.

00:24:10.012 --> 00:24:11.552
I guess I wanted to be popular.

00:24:12.636 --> 00:24:16.296
Oh, sure, but you didn't go around stealing things to make an impression.

00:24:16.956 --> 00:24:19.436
No, the worst thing I ever did was tell the other girls

00:24:19.436 --> 00:24:21.296
that John Bowles was my uncle.

00:24:22.476 --> 00:24:23.436
No, you didn't.

00:24:24.444 --> 00:24:25.244
Yes, I did.

00:24:25.692 --> 00:24:28.392
I'd even write myself letters and sign them, Uncle John.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.000
Well, come to think about it.

00:24:31.564 --> 00:24:34.264
I once autographed a baseball to myself, signed Gabby Hartnett.

00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:37.300
Only trouble was, I spelled heart in it wrong.
